gl5: the integrand was evaluated at the midpoint node

The control for `gauss_legendre_5_midpoint_node_neg`. The midpoint node is
the interesting one because no data dependency on `half_range` forces the
guard to precede it, so an expectation about that ordering has to show the
node runs at all. This integrand is silent everywhere except exactly 0.5, so
the trap firing here is evidence that `x3 = mid` is evaluated and that the
rule really does sample its midpoint.
